Done. Here's a summary of the two files:

**`SortableList.razor`** — Renders a `<ul>` with each item using your `ItemTemplate`, plus "Move Up" / "Move Down" buttons (disabled at boundaries). Uses `@key` for efficient diffing.

**`SortableList.razor.cs`** — Generic `partial class SortableList<TItem>`:
- Copies the incoming `Items` parameter into a private `_items` list in `OnParametersSet` (never mutates the caller's list).
- Swap logic in `MoveUp`/`MoveDown` then invokes `OnOrderChanged` with a read-only copy of the reordered list.

Usage matches your example—just use `OnOrderChanged` to receive the updated list:

```razor
<SortableList Items="@tasks" OnOrderChanged="HandleReorder">
    <ItemTemplate>
        <span>@context.Title</span>
    </ItemTemplate>
</SortableList>

@code {
    private void HandleReorder(IReadOnlyList<TaskItem> newOrder)
    {
        tasks = newOrder.ToList();
    }
}
```
